0,Puluwat language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puluwat_language,"November 22, 2025 - Puluwatese consists of long consonants ccòwo (heavy) and short consonants ppel (light). Long consonants are considered more forceful and are often used to display an emotion such as fear. Such an example is the word for hide-and seek/ tow-the-ghost: likohhomà.",Puluwatese,Austronesian
1,Austronesian peoples - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austronesian_peoples,1 week ago - Gong ensembles are also a common musical heritage of Island Southeast Asia. The casting of gong instruments is believed to have originated from the Bronze Age cultures of Mainland Southeast Asia. It spread to the Austronesian islands initially through trade as prestige goods.,Puluwatese,Austronesian
